  "Question": "\\(100\\times 19.98\\times 1.998\\times 1000=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((1.998)^2 \\)",
    "B": "\\((19.98)^2 \\)",
    "C": "\\((199.8)^2 \\)",
    "D": "\\((1998)^2 \\)",
    "E": "\\((19980)^2 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The choices are squares, so look for a way to make two equal factors. Multiplying \\(19.98\\) by \\(100\\) moves its decimal point two places right, and multiplying \\(1.998\\) by \\(1000\\) moves its decimal point three places right:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n100\\times19.98&=1998,\\\\\n1000\\times1.998&=1998.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nWe may change the order and grouping of factors in a product. Therefore the original expression equals \\(1998\\times1998=(1998)^2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
